  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 249 AM EDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nA weak cold front extends from Southern Ontario down through \nsouthern Lower MI, NW IN, and IL. Winds are light generally out of \nthe west, but becoming light/variable. Some BR/Patchy fog is \npossible early this morning, depending on how much clearing there is \nwith increasing cloud cover in the southwest. Expect a more \nnorthwest to north flow through the day, with light north-northeast \nflow becoming variable again tonight. Waves on Lake MI beaches this \nmorning will be around 2 feet, maybe a few up to 3 feet further \nnorth near St. Joseph, MI before subsiding to 1-2 feet later \nthis afternoon. Have a moderate swim risk for northern Berrien \ncounty, MI today, with breaking waves and currents expected. \nOtherwise, low swim risk conditions should persist further south\nas wave heights struggle to get above 2 feet. \n\nChances for showers and maybe a couple thunderstorms this afternoon \nas the cold front shifts E-SE and an upper level trough moves \nthrough. Most of the guidance remains south of US 30 (where we have \n20-50 percent chances), but a few models do kick of isolated showers \na bit further north-mainly along/south of US 24 in NW OH/NE IN. Kept \nfocus along/south of US 30 for now. Severe weather is not expected. \nSlightly cooler today, with highs in the upper 70s. \n\nHigh pressure/upper level ridge builds in tonight into Friday, with \na surface high in place. Expect highs around 80 degrees under mostly \nclear skies. Lows will be in the upper 50s, low 60s. \n\nThe next chances for rain return late Fri night into Saturday night \n(20-40 percent) as a shortwave/weak trough moves through fairly \nzonal flow. Zonal flow lingers through early next week, so have low \nchances (20 percent or less until Monday evening) to account for the \npotential, with highs in the low-mid 80s. Monday night into Thu a \nbroad frontal zone extends across our area, so have pops increasing \nonce again into the 30-50 percent range to account for that. Will \nlikely cover less time than forecasted, but there are uncertainties \nwith the exact location of the frontal zone and key upper level \nfeatures. Kept generic for now. Highs will be in the upper 70s, low \nto mid 80s for the most part. A few locations could reach 90 degrees \nMonday afternoon.",
